00:19:50,757 --> 00:19:53,257
needs it to run it, how does it do that?

343
00:19:53,577 --> 00:19:58,697
There's that do_nanosleep function in
the kernel, and this is its disassembly.

344
00:19:59,107 --> 00:20:02,847
The code that's actually in the
kernel, and you can see the first

345
00:20:02,847 --> 00:20:07,757
instruction here is the call, and it's
