00:20:10,267 --> 00:20:14,487
It literally goes to its own
code and modifies it at runtime.

348
00:20:14,927 --> 00:20:19,817
It adds a call instruction to what's
called a trampoline meaning that

349
00:20:19,817 --> 00:20:22,647
the moment that the do_nanosleep is
called, the kernel will execute the

350
00:20:22,647 --> 00:20:25,877
function, jump into my code, and
at the end of my code it jumps back

351
00:20:25,877 --> 00:20:27,787
to the beginning of do_nanosleep.

352
00:20:28,267 --> 00:20:33,277
And so the function we're looking or
hooking runs as if it were never there.

353
00:20:33,557 --> 00:20:40,597
And so now that my code is running BPF
code, not 686 like we see here we now

